# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Kept out of the release tarball, not out of the repository.
#
# GitHub builds its source downloads with `git archive`, which honours
# export-ignore, and Zenodo archives that download. At 405 MB the whole tree is
# more than the GitHub-to-Zenodo hand-off will carry; dropping these two leaves
# ~105 MB.
#
# What stays is chosen so the archive is still a working artefact rather than
# just citable source: sample_eval, sample_test and all three checkpoints remain,
# so `python demo.py` and `python evaluate.py` run from it and reproduce the
# reference table in the README.
#
# What goes is what only the two things a reviewer is least likely to run need:
#   data/live/                 the projection clips - `--live`, `Data.py record`
#                              and `make_light` only. README_data already says a
#                              copy that neither collects nor projects can delete
#                              them.
#   SampleData/sample_train/   179 MB, read by `train.py` and nothing else. The
#                              shipped checkpoint is what the paper reports; the
#                              training split is for retraining it.
#
# `git clone` is unaffected and still carries everything.
data/live export-ignore
data/SampleData/sample_train export-ignore
